# Workflow Skills — Specification Index

## 1. How to use

- **Index (this file):** High-level roadmap, phase feature map, next specs, done log.
- **Detail specs (`*.spec.md`):** Deep requirements and acceptance criteria in `.agents/specs/`.

## 2. Status legend

| Mark | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `[ ]` | todo |
| `[~]` | partial |
| `[x]` | done |
| `Verified: ...` | optional host smoke — **never auto-written by sync** |

## 3. Goal

Provide agent- and IDE-neutral workflow skills, orchestrators, and utility skills for coding assistants, enabling seamless spec-to-PR delivery, code review, verification, and harness maintenance across repositories.

## 4. Problems

- LLM agents often produce scope creep, over-complicated edits, or unverified claims.
- Delivery pipelines (spec generation, planning, implementation, review, testing, PR creation) are often monolithic or hardcoded to specific IDEs.
- Consumer projects need managed skill installation with customizable local project configurations.

## 5. Primary use cases

- **UC1:** End-to-end automated software delivery using `ws-spec-to-pr` or `ws-spec-to-pr-lite`.
- **UC2:** Batch execution of multiple specs sequentially with `ws-multi-spec`.
- **UC3:** Harness integrity scanning and verification via `ws-check-harness` and `ws-check-workflows`.
- **UC4:** Opt-in adversarial verification and domain reasoning via `ws-fable-judge` and `ws-fable-domain`.

## 6. Constraints & non-goals

- Skills must remain host-neutral and portable across IDEs/agents without product-specific hardcoding.
- Consumer `shared/` configurations (`config.json`, `STACK.md`, `MEMORY.md`) are consumer-owned and never overwritten on upstream updates.

## 7. Feature map by phase

### Phase 1: Core Foundation & Provider Abstractions
- [x] Provider skills for spec-to-pr (GitHub, Azure DevOps, local specs) (`spec: spec-provider-skills.spec.md`)
- [x] Promote shared skills to first-class installable packages (`spec: promote-shared-skills.spec.md`)
- [x] Skill install checksum integrity (SHA-256 digests + install gate) (`spec: skill-install-checksums/step-00-skill-install-checksums.spec.md`)

### Phase 2: System Quality & Integration
- [x] Consolidated GitHub Issues Fix: #106, #109, and #110 (`spec: consolidated-gh-issues.spec.md`)
- [x] Opt-in Integration of fable-* Skills with spec-to-pr Workflows (`spec: fable-skills-integration.spec.md`)

### Phase 3: Continuous Verification & Advanced Quality Gates
- [ ] Continuous AI Verification & Quality Gates Engine (`spec: continuous-ai-verification-quality-gates.spec.md`)
- [x] GraphQL Thread Resolution & Verification in `ws-goal-fix-pr` (`spec: us-168-resolve-review-thread.spec.md`)
- [x] Source-of-Truth Refactoring to `src/` & Hybrid Global Mode (`spec: src-sot-and-hybrid-global-install.spec.md`)
- [x] Mandatory Workflow Git Cleanup & Protected Branch Safeguards (`spec: workflow-cleanup-and-branch-protection.spec.md`)
- [x] Skill Authoring Guidelines & Global Config Gate Rules (`spec: skill-authoring-and-config-gate-rules.spec.md`)
- [x] Dual-Board Spec & Plan Management via `ws-spec-list` (`spec: ws-spec-list-and-board-management.spec.md`)
- [x] Remove Consumer Requirement for packaged `.agents/AGENTS.md`; consumer hub is `ws-shared/` (optional root `AGENTS.md` via autoload) (`spec: remove-consumer-agents-md-requirement.spec.md`)
- [x] Shared `autoload.md` + configure-project root `AGENTS.md` generation (`spec: shared-autoload-md.spec.md`)
- [x] Always-applied skills overlap audit & thin complementarity edits (`spec: autoload-skills-overlap-audit.spec.md`)
- [x] Fix broken `../ws-shared/` links in classify THRESHOLDS.md (`spec: us-183.spec.md`)
- [x] Opt-in mutation testing gate in Spec-to-PR Step 7 (`spec: workflow-mutation-testing-gate.spec.md`)
- [x] Configurable delivery-commit artifacts (`defaults.deliveryCommitArtifacts`) (`spec: configurable-delivery-commit-artifacts.spec.md`)
- [x] Configurable consumer autoload flag (`defaults.autoload` + harness enforce) (`spec: configurable-consumer-autoload.spec.md`)
- [x] Project Patterns Memory Skills (`ws-patterns-backend` & `ws-patterns-frontend`) (`spec: project-patterns-memory-skills.spec.md`)

